            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SPEARFISHER"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really enjoyed this. A good friend of mine is Columbian and offered this as a alternative to chimichurri. It has WAAY less fat than chimichurri and it tastes great. It is better to make it ahead of time though. That way the flavors have time to mix. I grilled a flank steak and used this on the steak after it was cooked. Thanks!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gordon Haave"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made about 6 batches of this. Love it! This latest time I left out the water and I added 4 habeneros to kick it up a notch. Best batch yet.",
            "datePublished": "2017-07-04T14:43:37.870Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BAREFOOTLADY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wonderful stuff - just like the green sauce at a South American restaurant we enjoy eating at. Not too hot if you remove the seeds and very easy to make. I left the seeds in once and it was too hot so we toned it down with some roasted tomatillos and poblano peppers and it was good with those additions too. But the recipe as written is definitely 5 stars in my book - only change I made was leaving out the water, as it was perfect consistency without it.",
            "datePublished": "2014-07-06T12:27:46.740Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jane Allen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "OMG t5his is so good!. I was very skeptical but I decided to make it for South American Pot luck. I did add about 4 cloves of garlic and subbed 1/2 of a red onion and a shallot because I didn't have green onions. kept everything else the same. It has a great bright flavor and I can't wait to bring it tomorrow. We just ate it on chips. It would be fantastic on steak or a steak taco, fish or shrimp taco too.",
            "datePublished": "2015-09-15T19:08:14.250Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Richard B"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My Colombian friends fell in love with this recipe. They can't get enough of it. I made one change that they liked . I use a 1-1 blend of pasilla and jalapeno peppers. Gives a bit more flavor and a bit less heat. The final product needs to be on the salty side.",
            "datePublished": "2015-02-28T19:36:27.420Z"
          },
          {
